          ":question/math-academy-id": "q-47587",
          ":question/problem": "Consider the following sentence:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $det(A)=0,$ then $\\underline{\\phantom{xxxxxx}}\\,.$*\n\nWhich of the following can be placed into the blank space to make a true statement?\n\nSelect all that apply.",
          ":question/worked-solution": "The invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$A$ is invertible $\\,\u21d4\\,\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}\\text{Col}(A) &={R}^{n} \\\\ \\text{dim(Col}(A)) &=n=\\text{rank}(A) \\\\ \\text{Null}(A) &=\\{0\\} \\\\ \\text{dim(Null}(A)) &=0=\\text{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}\\right.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the options separately.\n\n- The following statement is true:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $det(A)=0,$ then $A$ has no inverse.* $\\,\u2713$  \n\nIndeed,  a matrix $A$ is invertible if and only if $det(A)\\ne 0.$\n\n- The following statement is false:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $det(A)=0,$ then $\\text{rank}(A)=n.$*$\\,\\times$\n\nSince our matrix is not invertible, according to the invertible matrix theorem, it must be $\\text{rank}(A)\\ne n.$\n\n- The following statement is false:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $det(A)=0,$ then all columns of $A$ are pivot columns.*  $\\,\\times$\n\nSince $\\text{rank}(A)\\ne n$, it must be $\\text{dim(Col}(A))<n,$ which means that not all columns of $A$ are pivot columns.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \u201c$A$ has no inverse\u201d only."
        },
